# Nest modules

## Global infra

`DrizzleModule`, `MediaModule`, `PubSubModule` are `@Global()`. Domain modules do not re-import them to inject `DrizzleService` / `MediaStorageService`.

`TusModule.registerAsync` and CORS `registerAsync` run at **`apps/api`**. Feature modules register strategies on a registry (`TusHandlerRegistry`) in `onModuleInit`.

## `registerAsync` + tokens

```ts
export const TUS_OPTIONS = Symbol('TUS_OPTIONS');

TusModule.registerAsync({
  imports: [...mediaEnvFromConfig.imports],
  inject: [...mediaEnvFromConfig.inject],
  useFactory: (media: ConfigType<typeof mediaConfig>) => ({
    root: media.tusRoot,
    path: TusConfig.PATH,
    maxUploadBytes: SpaceConfig.FILE_MAX_BYTES,
  }),
});
```

Env factories use `registerAs` + `.asProvider()`. Shared async options type: `RegisterAsyncOptions`. Tokens live in `tokens/` as `Symbol`s.

## Roots vs feature

| At `apps/api` | In the domain module |
| --- | --- |
| `ConfigModule.forRoot` | `ConfigModule.forFeature` when injecting a namespaced config |
| `BullModule.forRootAsync` | `BullModule.registerQueue` |
| `ScheduleModule.forRoot` | `@Cron` providers |
| `TusModule.registerAsync` | `TusUploadHandler` + `registry.register` |

Do not call `forRoot` from `SpacesModule` — a second domain would fight the singleton root.

## Providers

Default **singleton** scope (`nest-singleton.mdc`). Request-scoped pipes (`ShareSessionPipe`) are the exception. GraphQL resolvers stay singleton: `AuthoredSpace` reads cookies from the execution context instead of injecting `REQUEST`.

Related: `nest-layers.mdc`, `nest-strategy.mdc`, `nest-singleton.mdc`.
